; newgameintro.eval - a new game opens with its opening lines wherever the
; party was (code-review C364). Judged by tools/WorldTest.py phase 22.
;
; StartNewGame returned as soon as it had to LOAD the level it opens on, and
; that load's completion only cleared the log - so Start New Game from crypt2
; began in silence, while the same start on the level already in hand showed
; the opening. Three readouts of the HUD's message log:
;   1. a new game on the harness level, already in hand - the opening (what
;      the third must show);
;   2. after `goto crypt2`, a plain level change - an empty log, so whatever
;      the third shows is not the first one's lines left over;
;   3. a new game from crypt2, which has to load the harness level first.
logecho on
reset
echo --- intro: in hand ---
newgame
messages 6
echo --- intro: after a goto ---
goto crypt2
messages 6
echo --- intro: from crypt2 ---
newgame
messages 6
state
